ok: a test declaring the dep
ok: a test omitting the dep
ok: a test with deps but not this one
ok: the dep is found wherever in deps it sits
ok: an explicit file dependency declares it
ok: the shared source config is not the local one
ok: so does one bound to a name
ok: an alias of the same name is not the file
ok: nor is an environment variable of that name
ok: a glob does not depend on the copied config
ok: a multi-test stanza is one site naming both
ok: inline tests declare the dep inside their own field
ok: an inline-test field with no deps at all
ok: a library's own deps are not the inline tests' deps
ok: a plain library is not a site
ok: an executable is not a site
ok: a rule running an executable is a site
ok: a rule running an executable through a named dep is one too
ok: a named dep may wrap its path in a dependency form
ok: a named dep resolving to no executable is not evidence of an external tool
ok: a chdir moves the directory whose config matters
ok: and the dependency that satisfies it is the one reaching that directory
ok: a test's own action can move where it runs
ok: a test with an ordinary action still runs where it is
ok: an explicit relative program is a site without an extension
ok: a bare word is still a tool on PATH
ok: a chdir to the stanza's own directory changes nothing
ok: a nested action does not hide the executable
ok: a rule running no executable is not a site
ok: a rule running a non-OCaml tool is not a site
ok: an alias stanza is read like a rule
ok: a public executable through %{bin:...}
ok: %{exe:...} names one too
ok: a shell action is not parsed, it is reported
ok: including one where a word split would have lost the executable
ok: a rule that copies an executable does not run it
ok: a command this scan cannot place is reported, not ignored
ok: dynamic-run executes a program as much as run does
ok: an action head on neither list is reported
ok: a program action's arguments are not actions
ok: an executable elsewhere keeps its path
ok: a filename's punctuation is part of its identity
ok: a toolchain pform runs a compiler, not a test
ok: a path built out of a pform is not guessed at
ok: a stanza inside a comment is not a stanza
ok: a config named in a comment does not declare it
ok: a config named in a string is not a dep
ok: an executable named in a comment does not make a rule a site
ok: a subdir's stanzas are the same kinds of site
ok: a nested subdir names the path it applies to
ok: stanzas outside the subdir keep the dune file's own directory
ok: stanzas are reported in file order
